WEBVTT

00:08.742 --> 00:16.783
Shiroi mikazuki machi wo miorosu koro ni

00:16.783 --> 00:24.781
Aoi meikyuu kara mashou ga mezame-hajimeru

00:32.298 --> 00:36.102
Tsumibukai kono chijou de, boy

00:36.102 --> 00:39.105
Believing, dreaming

00:39.105 --> 00:42.942
Boku-tachi wa sagashiteru

00:42.942 --> 00:48.073
Tamashii no mezasubeki basho wo

00:49.883 --> 00:58.291
Ah, dore kurai fukai yami hikari ni kaetara

00:58.291 --> 01:02.862
Sekai no iro ga kawaru?

01:02.862 --> 01:05.532
Ah, itsuka kitto

01:05.532 --> 01:13.807
Ah, dore kurai fukai nazo ikutsumo toitara

01:13.807 --> 01:18.767
Rakuen no doa wa hiraku?

01:20.313 --> 01:26.946
Bokura no tabi wo start hajimeyou

01:52.846 --> 01:54.143
This thing is...

01:59.085 --> 02:01.053
Loki? Where are you?

02:06.726 --> 02:07.693
Now!

02:18.872 --> 02:20.373
Oww...

02:20.373 --> 02:22.170
I twisted my ankle.

02:24.010 --> 02:26.379
What do we do? This vase looks expensive.

02:26.379 --> 02:30.179
Even Mayura can come in handy now and then.

02:30.483 --> 02:32.110
Right, Ecchan?

02:33.686 --> 02:39.420
The 4th Night
My Dad's a Great Detective?!

02:42.195 --> 02:43.463
Good grief!

02:43.463 --> 02:45.761
How long is Mayura going to
be out playing around?

02:46.466 --> 02:52.639
Don't tell me she's hanging around that
fishy detective agency again.

02:52.639 --> 02:53.936
I'm home!

02:56.142 --> 02:57.977
Where were you, Mayura?!

02:57.977 --> 03:00.707
I keep telling you to call if you're
going to be out late!

03:04.551 --> 03:06.178
Hello and good evening!

03:06.686 --> 03:07.812
Hiya!

03:10.757 --> 03:13.055
You morons!

03:15.061 --> 03:18.798
For the longest time, all you've been going on
about is "detective work" and "mysteries"

03:18.798 --> 03:21.096
and a bunch of other things
that make no sense.

03:21.568 --> 03:26.639
You're a high school student now, so you
need to take a good look at reality

03:26.639 --> 03:28.732
and start leaving this
fantastical stuff behind.

03:29.142 --> 03:31.878
My dad's sermons sure go on
for a long time, huh?

03:31.878 --> 03:34.870
Why do I have to get chewed out too?

03:35.682 --> 03:38.583
Shut up and listen when people
are talking to you!

03:41.054 --> 03:42.555
Hey, Loki.

03:42.555 --> 03:48.516
Explain to my dad how much I really am
helping society as a detective.

03:48.928 --> 03:50.196
Why?

03:50.196 --> 03:53.633
'Cuz at this rate, he'll forbid
me from being one.

03:53.633 --> 03:56.936
You wouldn't want to lose such a
talented assistant, would you?

03:56.936 --> 03:58.904
C'mon! I'll buy you a pizza.

04:01.241 --> 04:02.765
Thanks, Loki!

04:03.109 --> 04:06.806
Mayura did help you out today, didn't she?

04:09.015 --> 04:12.285
What's more, you're obsessed with the
occult and all that mumbo-jumbo!

04:12.285 --> 04:15.521
But things like ghosts and
demons do not exist!

04:15.521 --> 04:18.183
It's all just lies and trickery!

04:18.391 --> 04:20.727
That's right. It's trickery.

04:20.727 --> 04:23.218
Of course there are no such things
as demons are there?

04:24.364 --> 04:26.666
Hello, is this Do-Re-Mi pizza?

04:26.666 --> 04:28.634
This is Daidoji Temple.

04:29.235 --> 04:31.738
I'd like to order a pizza for delivery.

04:31.738 --> 04:33.706
Ah, yes.

04:34.107 --> 04:35.734
The cheapest one.

04:37.277 --> 04:39.646
Hey, Loki, it comes with ice cream.

04:39.646 --> 04:41.944
Do you want vanilla or strawberry?

04:43.583 --> 04:45.380
Are you going to order anything, Dad?

04:46.586 --> 04:48.520
Dad... What's wrong?

04:49.789 --> 04:52.692
I won't have you playing around
in the occult any longer!

04:52.692 --> 04:54.894
And you are forbidden from going to
that detective agency again!

04:54.894 --> 04:57.021
Huh? But why?

04:57.497 --> 04:59.965
That's enough for today.
Finish your homework and go to bed!

05:00.533 --> 05:02.000
Wait, Dad!

05:11.144 --> 05:12.270
Dad?

05:14.247 --> 05:18.384
I've had enough!
As of today, no more allowance!

05:18.384 --> 05:21.254
This seems to have turned into
an even bigger mess.

05:21.254 --> 05:22.346
Oh well. I guess there's no choice.

05:49.048 --> 05:49.844
What's that?

05:59.792 --> 06:01.419
What was that just now?

06:02.995 --> 06:04.462
Where are we?

06:09.235 --> 06:10.370
Is that...

06:10.370 --> 06:12.972
Could that be me when I was little?

06:12.972 --> 06:16.100
Is that me when I was young?

06:21.414 --> 06:24.317
Master Loki, what is this place?

06:24.317 --> 06:27.387
This is the world inside their memories.

06:27.387 --> 06:29.088
Inside their memories?

06:29.088 --> 06:34.025
I brought us all into the memories of Mayura
and her father from ten years ago.

06:35.395 --> 06:37.897
This is a dream!

06:37.897 --> 06:41.200
I must have fallen asleep
without realizing it.

06:41.200 --> 06:42.702
Hey, Dad!

06:42.702 --> 06:45.405
This Cat Detective is MEOWvelous!

06:45.405 --> 06:46.038
Cat Detective
This Cat Detective is MEOWvelous!

06:46.038 --> 06:48.029
Cat Detective
He can figure out anything!

06:48.274 --> 06:50.765
Mayura's so cute!

06:51.811 --> 06:54.547
Oh, yeah? That's great.

06:54.547 --> 06:57.243
Dad's so young!

06:58.284 --> 06:59.952
The Cat Detective, huh?

06:59.952 --> 07:03.046
This was when I started
getting into detectives.

07:03.556 --> 07:07.720
Hey, Dad, how can I meet a real detective?

07:08.561 --> 07:10.296
A detective?

07:10.296 --> 07:12.594
I'm sure you'll be able to meet one
as long as you're a good girl.

07:13.132 --> 07:15.134
Hey, younger me!

07:15.134 --> 07:18.592
If you say things like that, Mayura will
start developing some bizarre interests!

07:19.172 --> 07:20.706
Now, now, Mayura!

07:20.706 --> 07:23.607
How about we do something more fun
than this detective stuff?

07:31.617 --> 07:34.020
I guess this is some kind of dream after all.

07:34.020 --> 07:37.751
It looks like our old selves
can't see us right now.

07:38.090 --> 07:41.794
By the way, what do you want
for your birthday?

07:41.794 --> 07:46.299
Hmm... I want to get a pat on
the head by the beanstalk.

07:46.299 --> 07:48.597
A pat on the head by the beanstalk?!

07:50.470 --> 07:52.872
A pat on the head by the beanstalk, huh?

07:52.872 --> 07:56.273
Well, we have plenty of pines and
cedars here at the temple.

07:56.576 --> 07:58.711
No, no that.

07:58.711 --> 08:00.847
A pat on the head by the beanstalk.

08:00.847 --> 08:03.649
Okay, got it. I'll figure something out.

08:03.649 --> 08:05.776
A pat by the beanstalk, right?

08:08.454 --> 08:09.318
Okay!

08:10.623 --> 08:13.091
How come he understood that just now?

08:13.493 --> 08:16.762
I think I smell a mystery!

08:16.762 --> 08:19.765
Okay, I'm going to go find a beanstalk.

08:19.765 --> 08:21.562
Now you be a good girl.

08:23.469 --> 08:25.471
The riddles are calling to me!

08:25.471 --> 08:27.473
Wait!

08:27.473 --> 08:29.100
Whoa! Hold on, Mayura!

08:31.177 --> 08:32.940
Hey, where are you going?

08:34.213 --> 08:36.482
It's dangerous to go out on your own.

08:36.482 --> 08:38.780
Wait, Mayura. Mayura!

08:40.253 --> 08:42.380
What's a beanstalk anyhow?

08:43.890 --> 08:46.859
Isn't there anything here that
might give me a hint?

08:48.094 --> 08:51.931
Jeez, he didn't understand after all!

08:51.931 --> 08:53.899
He got my hopes up for nothing!

09:00.940 --> 09:04.398
If you were here, I bet you'd
have known right away.

09:05.845 --> 09:09.474
That's right. By that point,
Mom wasn't around anymore.

09:09.715 --> 09:11.615
By "not around," you mean...

09:12.785 --> 09:15.253
What are you two doing here?

09:15.588 --> 09:16.756
Shock!

09:16.756 --> 09:20.055
Um, well... It's a dream!

09:20.660 --> 09:22.287
Oh, okay.

09:24.931 --> 09:29.231
My mom fell ill and died
when I was very little.

09:31.604 --> 09:36.098
Mayura's still so little. It seems she
doesn't understand you died.

09:36.676 --> 09:41.080
Even now, she'll ask where you are
and start looking for you.

09:41.080 --> 09:43.378
I don't know how to explain it to her.

09:44.150 --> 09:45.447
Dad...

09:51.657 --> 09:54.794
Mayura, it's dangerous to go
out walking alone.

09:54.794 --> 09:56.785
I think it's about time you head home.

10:01.000 --> 10:04.333
If I plant these beans in the ground,
I wonder if a beanstalk will grow out...

10:05.338 --> 10:06.703
It won't, it won't!

10:07.540 --> 10:10.142
Oh. Hi there, Mayura! On your own today?

10:10.142 --> 10:13.779
Yeah! I don't want to get in
the way of my dad's work!

10:13.779 --> 10:15.681
You're such a good girl!

10:15.681 --> 10:18.117
Still, it must be lonely now
that your mother's gone.

10:18.117 --> 10:22.315
It's okay! She made a promise
to me for my birthday.

10:24.223 --> 10:27.021
Where are you going now, Mayura?

10:29.962 --> 10:31.864
Hello, Mr. Panda.

10:31.864 --> 10:33.456
I came to see you again!

10:33.933 --> 10:35.423
Mr. Panda?

10:36.802 --> 10:38.929
She must mean that stuffed animal.

10:39.338 --> 10:43.638
Why don't you come with me to the
amusement park next time, okay?

10:44.443 --> 10:45.910
Mayura!

10:47.513 --> 10:48.480
Mayura!

10:48.948 --> 10:50.416
Where are you?

10:50.416 --> 10:51.417
Where did you go?

10:51.417 --> 10:53.749
Where are you, Mayura?

10:57.056 --> 10:58.683
Wait, Dad!

10:59.792 --> 11:02.294
Well, now. They've finally started
getting a move on, have they?

11:02.294 --> 11:03.929
Let's go, Yamino.

11:03.929 --> 11:05.226
Yes, Master Loki.

11:41.100 --> 11:43.302
Interested in books from a very young age.

11:43.302 --> 11:45.071
That's my girl!

11:45.071 --> 11:47.699
Yes, they certainly are the
cornerstone of education.

11:48.374 --> 11:51.502
Hey, Mister, where are the detective books?

11:51.644 --> 11:53.111
Detective?!

11:53.512 --> 11:56.640
Our mystery novel section
is right over there.

11:56.882 --> 11:58.372
The Great Detective

12:01.587 --> 12:04.523
Mayura, you don't have to
read mystery novels!

12:04.523 --> 12:07.754
There are plenty of other books out there
that are more interesting!

12:07.960 --> 12:12.988
Hey, Mister, how do detectives
go searching for someone?

12:13.299 --> 12:17.670
They probably start by investigating the
places where that person went a lot.

12:17.670 --> 12:21.504
If it's a fun place, the person
might still be going there.

12:21.941 --> 12:24.739
Don't go giving my daughter
more stupid ideas!

12:25.311 --> 12:26.979
I'm gonna go check it out!

12:26.979 --> 12:28.378
Mayura, wait!

12:28.781 --> 12:29.014
GREENGROCER

12:29.014 --> 12:31.539
GREENGROCER
What? Mayura was here?

12:31.817 --> 12:34.615
Yeah, she was looking at those beans.

12:34.987 --> 12:37.888
I guess she really is searching
for a beanstalk.

12:38.257 --> 12:40.259
Which way did she go?

12:40.259 --> 12:42.461
That I don't know.

12:42.461 --> 12:45.225
But, she said something about
a promise for her birthday.

12:45.765 --> 12:47.562
A promise for her birthday?

12:48.267 --> 12:49.461
Could it be...

12:53.839 --> 12:55.864
I thought she might be here.

12:56.342 --> 12:58.810
Hey, I still have this stuffed animal!

12:59.111 --> 13:03.844
Mayura had her mother promise to
buy it as a birthday present.

13:04.950 --> 13:06.918
That's right...

13:07.653 --> 13:11.316
I remember she planted herself here
and threw a tantrum.

13:13.225 --> 13:16.529
She told her mom, "Mr. Panda is saying
he wants to be with me."

13:16.529 --> 13:19.098
And then her mom told her
the panda had said,

13:19.098 --> 13:24.502
"I'm going to come visit you on
your birthday. Just wait."

13:27.373 --> 13:28.499
Mom...

13:29.041 --> 13:32.340
She was good at coming up with
stories and fooling people.

13:32.778 --> 13:35.303
Even I've had the wool pulled over my eyes.

13:35.648 --> 13:39.106
Jeez, Dad! You're so insensitive!

13:39.351 --> 13:41.153
Mayura?

13:41.153 --> 13:43.222
No, I haven't seen her today.

13:43.222 --> 13:44.723
I see...

13:44.723 --> 13:48.352
She's probably playing "detective"
with her friends somewhere.

13:49.161 --> 13:52.619
That seems to be what the kids
around here are into lately.

13:53.265 --> 13:54.934
Playing "detective," huh?

13:54.934 --> 13:56.959
Maybe she's been reading that
picture book too much.

13:57.269 --> 14:00.067
Picture book?
Does he mean "The Cat Detective"?

14:00.973 --> 14:05.501
It's the last thing her mother bought for her,
so I can't tell her to stop reading it.

14:08.514 --> 14:11.317
"Then the Cat Detective said,

14:11.317 --> 14:14.253
'My eyes can see even in the dark

14:14.253 --> 14:18.883
and they can easily see through the
darkness of this case too!"'

14:19.625 --> 14:22.761
Wow, the Cat Detective is great!

14:22.761 --> 14:24.729
He knows everything!

14:24.997 --> 14:26.832
Yes, he certainly is great.

14:26.832 --> 14:31.370
Maybe he'd even know a way
to make you all better.

14:31.370 --> 14:33.439
Hmm, I wonder.

14:33.439 --> 14:38.809
But you know, as long as you'll be a
good girl, that's all I need to feel better.

14:39.144 --> 14:40.145
Really?

14:40.145 --> 14:41.203
Really.

14:42.081 --> 14:44.149
I'll be a good girl.

14:44.149 --> 14:45.946
I'll try my very best.

14:47.319 --> 14:48.718
Mom...

14:52.391 --> 14:54.859
What a kind mother she had.

14:57.563 --> 15:00.191
Mayura came here earlier.

15:01.066 --> 15:02.067
Really?

15:02.067 --> 15:05.638
She asked me how detectives
go about searching for people.

15:05.638 --> 15:09.597
I said that they start by going to the
places the person often visited.

15:10.542 --> 15:14.603
Don't go giving my daughter stupid ideas!

15:15.648 --> 15:17.783
So where did she go then?

15:17.783 --> 15:21.150
I said to try a fun place the
person often visited!

15:21.820 --> 15:24.880
A fun place that Mayura often visited?

15:25.658 --> 15:27.285
Mayura?

15:27.660 --> 15:29.560
No, she hasn't been here today.

15:30.529 --> 15:32.759
Maybe she went somewhere else.

15:32.898 --> 15:34.365
Where are you?

15:35.234 --> 15:36.360
Mayura!

15:37.136 --> 15:38.262
Dad...

15:45.277 --> 15:47.713
Where did she go?

15:47.713 --> 15:49.146
Oh, Mr. Daidoji!

15:50.115 --> 15:52.718
I ran into Mayura a little earlier.

15:52.718 --> 15:55.688
Really? Where did she go?

15:55.688 --> 15:58.953
She said she was going to go have
her mother pat her on the head.

16:01.760 --> 16:02.988
Ah.

16:05.331 --> 16:07.733
So that's what it was.

16:07.733 --> 16:09.963
Why didn't I realize it sooner?

16:10.402 --> 16:11.699
Mayura!

16:12.071 --> 16:13.038
Dad!

16:14.006 --> 16:15.303
There it is!

16:18.644 --> 16:20.544
This is...

16:20.746 --> 16:22.581
the amusement park?

16:22.581 --> 16:25.484
The three of us used to come here a lot.

16:25.484 --> 16:25.684
JACK AND THE BEANSTALK

16:25.684 --> 16:27.820
JACK AND THE BEANSTALK
Jack and the Beanstalk?

16:27.820 --> 16:27.920
Jack and the Beanstalk?

16:27.920 --> 16:30.089
So this is what she meant by beanstalk?

16:30.089 --> 16:30.422
UNDER CONSTRUCTION
So this is what she meant by beanstalk?

16:30.422 --> 16:30.789
UNDER CONSTRUCTION

16:30.789 --> 16:32.791
UNDER CONSTRUCTION
It says "under construction."

16:32.791 --> 16:33.052
UNDER CONSTRUCTION

16:33.459 --> 16:36.360
Mayura, you'll just have to find
a different ride for today.

16:37.696 --> 16:40.290
Mayura, wait! It's dangerous! Come back!

16:51.276 --> 16:52.743
That's dangerous, Mayura!

16:59.318 --> 17:00.785
Wow, there's so many!

17:03.188 --> 17:04.757
For crying out loud.

17:04.757 --> 17:06.486
Why'd she have to come here?

17:06.658 --> 17:09.491
Mom's waiting by the exit, isn't she?

17:10.863 --> 17:14.533
'Cuz Mom was always waiting by the exit.

17:14.533 --> 17:19.493
Say "welcome back" and pat me on the
head like you always do, okay?

17:20.239 --> 17:21.536
Mayura...

17:22.841 --> 17:22.908
Exit

17:22.908 --> 17:24.176
Exit
Mom!

17:24.777 --> 17:28.008
Welcome back! You did a good job!

17:32.284 --> 17:35.913
Mom, I'll do a good job,
so just wait for me!

17:37.623 --> 17:41.320
This is what she meant by getting a pat
on the head by the beanstalk.

17:44.630 --> 17:46.257
There's the exit!

17:46.832 --> 17:48.299
Mom!

17:49.868 --> 17:51.335
Mayura, watch out!

17:55.040 --> 17:56.166
Mayura!

17:57.543 --> 17:59.044
Are you all right, Mayura?

17:59.044 --> 18:00.409
Are you hurt?

18:01.613 --> 18:03.672
Oww. It stings.

18:03.982 --> 18:05.851
Oh, does it hurt?

18:05.851 --> 18:07.853
Poor Mayura.

18:07.853 --> 18:10.913
Boo-boo, boo-boo, go away! Go away!

18:17.529 --> 18:19.497
That's dangerous, Mayura! Stop!

18:20.032 --> 18:20.896
Mayura!

18:21.300 --> 18:22.835
See now?

18:22.835 --> 18:25.838
I told you so. Don't overdo it like that!

18:25.838 --> 18:28.407
I'm sure somebody will come
find you soon enough.

18:28.407 --> 18:31.710
Mom, I can't make it to the exit.

18:31.710 --> 18:32.938
Mom...

18:34.613 --> 18:36.782
I'm no good.

18:36.782 --> 18:39.351
I didn't try hard enough.

18:39.351 --> 18:41.819
So Mom won't come to see me.

18:42.154 --> 18:43.280
Mayura...

18:43.722 --> 18:44.848
Mom...

18:45.157 --> 18:46.658
That's not true!

18:46.658 --> 18:49.126
It's not your fault, Mayura!

18:49.661 --> 18:53.031
You're a good girl, and you
always do your best.

18:53.031 --> 18:55.659
You always give it your all.

18:56.401 --> 18:59.859
You're my little girl, my pride and joy.

19:01.073 --> 19:04.372
Mom... Come and see me. Mom...

19:06.178 --> 19:07.645
Mayura!

19:07.980 --> 19:08.947
Dad?

19:11.383 --> 19:13.977
Can't Dad take Mom's place?

19:15.988 --> 19:16.955
Dad?

19:21.493 --> 19:24.830
You make me worry when you go out
without saying anything.

19:24.830 --> 19:26.457
I'm sorry!

19:27.766 --> 19:31.703
You're not the only one who's
lonely now that Mom's gone.

19:31.703 --> 19:35.332
If you went away on me too,
I don't know what I'd do.

19:39.912 --> 19:43.015
Well, we came all the way to
the amusement park,

19:43.015 --> 19:45.150
so how about we ride the
merry-go-round or something?

19:45.150 --> 19:46.117
Okay!

19:48.387 --> 19:50.014
Hey, Dad.

19:51.123 --> 19:54.752
How did you know where I was?

19:56.261 --> 19:57.728
Well...

19:58.730 --> 20:00.698
It's because your dad is a great detective.

20:08.240 --> 20:09.908
Now I remember!

20:09.908 --> 20:14.446
This is when I decided I'd be a
detective when I grow up.

20:14.446 --> 20:16.114
What?!

20:16.114 --> 20:18.582
So then, it's all because of me?

20:27.826 --> 20:29.453
Like parent, like child, huh?

20:30.662 --> 20:31.788
Master Loki?

20:53.685 --> 20:55.312
It was a dream?

21:01.827 --> 21:03.522
Umm... Dad?

21:03.862 --> 21:05.693
What is it, Mayura?

21:06.031 --> 21:09.034
Well, it seems they're on better terms now.

21:09.034 --> 21:11.229
Good grief. They certainly are a handful.

21:13.772 --> 21:15.933
Oh, it sounds like my pizza's here!

21:18.277 --> 21:19.244
What was that?

21:23.048 --> 21:25.414
Rule #1 of the Mighty Part-timer:

21:25.584 --> 21:27.745
Make the delivery on time!

21:28.754 --> 21:29.982
My pizza...

21:30.289 --> 21:34.526
Sheesh. Is this the only kind of person
that Mayura hangs out with?

21:34.526 --> 21:36.721
Um, Dad?

21:38.297 --> 21:41.494
I'm sorry I got you so worried.

21:41.833 --> 21:44.301
Uh. Ah, well...

21:45.637 --> 21:47.306
Hey, what are you gonna do, right?

